<h1>PassiveRichTextEditor</h1>

<p>
    The passive editor renders the same Quill editor without registering change callbacks. Edits remain
    immediate in the browser, but values are sent to Blazor only when you request them. This avoids repeatedly
    transferring large documents or embedded images over JS interop, leading to a smoother experience when working
    with large documents.
</p>

<h2 id="on_demand_synchronization">On-demand synchronization</h2>

<p>
    Capture a component reference and call <code>UpdateContentAsync</code>, <code>UpdateTextAsync</code>, or
    <code>UpdateSelectionAsync</code> to refresh bound values. The corresponding <code>Get…Async</code> methods
    return a value without updating the binding.
</p>

<ExampleView TComponent="PassiveEditorExample">
    <PassiveEditorExample />
</ExampleView>

<h2 id="choosing_an_editor">Choosing an editor</h2>

<p>
    Prefer <code>RichTextEditor</code> for normal forms and reactive validation. Choose
    <code>PassiveRichTextEditor</code> when the document is large or synchronization should happen only at a
    save, preview, or validation boundary.
</p>
